B.dFr={skin:0,muscle:1,organ:2,bone:3}
B.aPe=new A.jS("Skin","Cover",0.115,0.52,"Your biggest organ. It keeps water in and germs out, and sheds about 30,000 dead cells every minute.",0)
B.aP8=new A.jS("Eyes","Senses",0,0.058,"Your eyes turn light into signals for the brain. Each sends the picture upside down and the brain flips it.",4)
B.aPl=new A.jS("Ears","Senses",0.045,0.062,"Ears hear and also keep your balance. The three tiny bones inside are the smallest in your body.",7)
B.aPg=new A.jS("Hair","Cover",0,0.012,"You have about 100,000 hairs on your head. Each grows about a centimetre a month.",9)
B.aPi=new A.jS("Hands","Touch",0.175,0.51,"Each hand has 27 bones and thousands of touch sensors. Your fingertips are among the most sensitive spots.",12)
B.aPp=new A.jS("Feet","Balance",0.055,0.975,"Each foot has 26 bones and about 250,000 sweat glands. Together they carry your whole weight.",14)
B.cOH=s([B.aPe,B.aP8,B.aPl,B.aPg,B.aPi,B.aPp],t.t_)
B.aP4=new A.jS("Chest muscles","Movement",0.05,0.2,"The pectoral muscles push your arms forward, like when you push a door.",0)
B.aPr=new A.jS("Biceps","Movement",0.14,0.27,"The biceps bends your elbow. When a muscle works it gets shorter and fatter.",4)
B.aP7=new A.jS("Abs","Movement",0,0.33,"Your tummy muscles hold your body upright and help you twist and bend.",7)
B.aPk=new A.jS("Quadriceps","Movement",0.065,0.58,"The four big muscles at the front of your thigh. They are the strongest in your body for lifting weight.",9)
B.aPh=new A.jS("Calf","Movement",0.07,0.8,"The calf pushes you up on your toes when you walk, run and jump.",12)
B.aP9=new A.jS("Shoulders","Movement",0.125,0.185,"The deltoids lift your arms in every direction. Your shoulder is the most flexible joint you have.",14)
B.cYG=s([B.aP4,B.aPr,B.aP7,B.aPk,B.aPh,B.aP9],t.t_)
B.aPn=new A.jS("Brain","Nerves",0,0.05,"Weighs about 1.4 kg and uses a fifth of your energy. It has around 86 billion nerve cells.",0)
B.aPc=new A.jS("Lungs","Breathing",-0.05,0.215,"You breathe about 20,000 times a day. Spread flat, your lungs would cover a tennis court.",4)
B.aPt=new A.jS("Heart","Blood",0.014,0.238,"About the size of your fist. It beats around 100,000 times a day and pumps blood round a track 100,000 km long.",7)
B.aPj=new A.jS("Liver","Digestion",-0.04,0.3,"Cleans your blood and stores energy. It is the only organ that can grow back after damage.",9)
B.aP6=new A.jS("Stomach","Digestion",0.045,0.3,"Acid in your stomach could dissolve metal, but a thick layer of mucus protects it.",12)
B.aP3=new A.jS("Kidneys","Cleaning",0.045,0.335,"Clean about 180 litres of blood every day and turn the waste into urine.",14)
B.aPa=new A.jS("Intestines","Digestion",0,0.395,"Your small intestine is about 6 metres long, folded up in your tummy. Food stays for hours.",16)
B.cFO=s([B.aPn,B.aPc,B.aPt,B.aPj,B.aP6,B.aP3,B.aPa],t.t_)
B.aPs=new A.jS("Skull","Frame",0,0.05,"Your skull is made of 22 bones that protect your brain. Only the jaw can move.",0)
B.aPb=new A.jS("Spine","Frame",0,0.3,"The spine has 33 bones called vertebrae, stacked like beads, with soft discs between them.",4)
B.aPq=new A.jS("Ribs","Frame",-0.062,0.22,"You have 12 pairs of ribs. They make a cage that protects your heart and lungs and moves when you breathe.",7)
B.aPo=new A.jS("Collarbone","Frame",0.07,0.16,"The most often broken bone, and the only long bone that lies sideways.",9)
B.aP5=new A.jS("Arm bones","Frame",0.148,0.28,"The humerus is the upper arm bone. Below the elbow you have two bones, the radius and the ulna.",12)
B.aPd=new A.jS("Pelvis","Frame",0,0.475,"The pelvis holds up your body and protects organs in your tummy.",14)
B.aPf=new A.jS("Thigh bone","Frame",0.072,0.6,"The femur is the longest and strongest bone in your body, about a quarter of your height.",16)
B.aPm=new A.jS("Shin bone","Frame",0.065,0.82,"The tibia carries most of your weight below the knee.",19)
